### 4a. Two independent axes — do not conflate them

The terminal has **two separate states**, and the banner reports both:

| Axis | Question | Source | Can flip mid-session? |
|---|---|---|---|
| **OpenAlgo mode** | Where do ORDERS go? | `/api/v1/analyzer` | Yes — 2 s poll |
| **data_source** | Where do the PANELS' prices come from? | `POV_DASH_LIVE` env, read once at startup | No — fixed per process |

The dashboard is config-only, so its reads are **stubbed by default**. The normal live configuration is therefore **(OpenAlgo live, panels paper)** — and that is what it currently runs.

The banner in `ui/mode.py::banner_text` omits the panel clause **only when the two axes agree**. Every ambiguous combination states both:

```
openalgo=live     panels=paper  -> LIVE - REAL MONEY  |  PANELS: PAPER DATA (ORDER-PLACING DISABLED)
openalgo=live     panels=live   -> LIVE - REAL MONEY
openalgo=analyze  panels=paper  -> ANALYZER (SIMULATED)
openalgo=analyze  panels=live   -> ANALYZER (SIMULATED)  |  PANELS: LIVE SDK DATA
```

Showing only the mode would put a red "LIVE - REAL MONEY" banner over simulated charts — the two-surfaces-disagree failure this design prevents. `/pov/mode` returns `mode`, `data_source` and the composed `banner`, so a client can never reconstruct the wrong string.

- Set `POV_DASH_LIVE=1` to wire real candles/quotes into the panels (changes `data_source` to `live`). Without it, panels stay paper. This does NOT enable order placing — the terminal has no order path at all.
- Writes target the nested `pov` block when one exists (the block the reader prefers) — otherwise the value is a silent no-op.
- Shared kit: `Blue_engine/dashboard/ui/` (kpi, panel, table, log_view, inputs, mode, provider). Old hand-written theme CSS removed from `pages/theme.py` (now a shim).
